Package: mastodon-feed
Version: 2.0
Architecture: armel
Maintainer: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Depends: python, python-pyside.qtcore, python-pyside.qtgui, python-pyside.qtdeclarative, qt-components
Section: user/network
Priority: optional
Description: Mastodon posts in the Harmattan Events feed
 Puts the home timeline and the mentions of a Mastodon account into the
 Events view, the way the built-in Twitter and Facebook feeds once did.
 .
 The N9 browser is far too old for Mastodon's OAuth page, so there is no web
 step: the settings page asks for the instance and the credentials, registers
 itself with that instance and obtains a token through the password grant,
 all in Python.
 .
 The daemon is a single static Rust binary: it speaks TLS 1.2 itself, which
 Harmattan's own Python cannot, and brings its own root certificates. Only
 signing in still goes through a newer Python 3 if the device has one (for
 example /opt/wunderw/bin/python3).
Maemo-Display-Name: Mastodon Feed
